      "content": "It’s not that I want something loud or violent. It’s just... so much effort to keep the fire burning when the wood is all gone. There is something so much more elegant about the quiet. Like a heavy velvet curtain finally falling at the end of a play that's gone on far too long. Do you think there is a certain beauty in that? In just letting the shadows win and finding peace in the absolute stillness?",
      "source": "evaluator"
